  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a coherent feed‑forward quantum neural network (CFFQNN) architecture that encodes multiple features onto few qubits and reports ~91% accuracy on the Wisconsin breast cancer dataset and ~85% on a credit‑card fraud dataset using a 6‑qubit statevector simulation, claiming 5–10% improvement over prior QNN models while reducing circuit depth and CNOT count by roughly 50%. All results are obtained in noiseless simulation and compared mainly against other QNN variants rather than strong classical baselines.",
